    {
      "id": "evidence-001-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "Two independent bounds, because either alone would be weaker than it looks. (1) `Kernel::axiom_footprint` walks THIS declaration's transitive dependencies and prints an empty footprint column -- this is the kernel's `#print axioms`, and it is the check that matters, since an integer law IS still asserted (`Int.euclidean_decomposition`; it was 6 until lane int-remainder proved the `subNatNat` borrow, and the check mattered more then) and Int.add_neg could have reached for one and still type-checked. (2) `nat_axiom_inventory` reports `nat: axiom=0 opaque=0 quotient=0` for the development ZZ is constructed over, so the foundation admits no trusted declaration at all. Counting `Declaration::Axiom` alone would not have sufficed: `Opaque` has no proof body and `Quotient` admits `Quot.sound`, which is exactly the declaration the quotient-of-NxN construction would have added -- the enumeration covers all three kinds and reports zero for each.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
