    {
      "id": "evidence-002-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "A wrong `Int.add` would satisfy a wrong-but-provable `add_neg`, so the theorem alone does not pin the operation down. This test evaluates 16 additions and multiplications and 5 negations by kernel reduction against their normal forms, covering every sign combination including the borrow cases where `Int.subNatNat` has to decide which constructor the answer lands in (3 + (-3) = 0 and 1 + (-3) = -2 are both present).",
